Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO WITHIN A FRACTION OF A MILLIMETER OF INKED MARGINS   SEE NOTE   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   NOTE  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  The tumor focally displays a solid growth pattern  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 3 x 2 x 1 cm fragment of breast with a REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension  ill defined  firm  tan white mass less or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked margin  The entire mass is submitted in cassettes A through C  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes D and E  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA REMOVED_DATE CM  AWAITING PERMANENTS FOR CONFIRMATION  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  report_end , 0.
