Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 52 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING A SCLEROSING PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Due to marked stromal distortion within the sclerosing papilloma  the presence of invasion cannot be entirely excluded  The sclerosing papilloma is present at the inked margin  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of breast containing a multilobulated mass with several satellite nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm  Submitted entirely in A through G  Tissue taken for EM  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Dennis C Sgroi  M D  Eugene Francis Ruffolo  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  report_end , 0.
