REMOVED_CASE_ID JAYAWARDENE MAKEVITAGE 48 F  REG REF REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  WIC NEWTON CHEH EMILY M D                                                                                             Specimen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID SOUT Received  REMOVED_DATE  1307 Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Indeterminate right breast calcifications  rule out ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereo biopsies  right breast  and contains an aqua cassette which is designated on the specimen requisition form to contain the specimen microcalcifications  Within this aqua cassette is a REMOVED_DATE cm  long  REMOVED_DATE cm  in diameter yellowish red  firm  glistening needle biopsy  The specimen is marked with green ink  Also present free floating within the specimen container is a 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm  aggregate of yellowish red soft needle biopsies admixed with blood clot measuring REMOVED_DATE cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with green ink  Section code  1   tissue in aqua cassette with specimen microcalcifications   1X all  2   free floating tissue   1 agg  all  Total fixation time is 12 hours  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  needle core biopsies  Pools of mucin with microcalcifications and adjacent detached strips of epithelium  see note   Microcalcifications also identified in adipose tissue  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1217 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1220 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1223 PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  The specimen consists of mostly adipose tissue with scant benign breast ducts and lobules  Both blocks of tissue show pools of mucin  Microcalcifications are identified within the mucin and within the adipose tissue  Adjacent to the mucin and focally within the mucin are strips of detached  fairly benign appearing epithelium  Both blocks of tissue have been completely leveled through  The pools of mucin are worrisome for mucinous carcinoma  however  a diagnosis of mucinous carcinoma cannot be made on this material given the lack of atypical epithelial cells within the mucin  Radiographic pathologic correlation is recommended and repeat biopsies may be indicated  especially if a mass lesion is identified  Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D  DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT   Continued  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1223 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1308 MD MIHN Notes  REMOVED_DATE  In addition to the cosigner Dr  Abbott  Dr  Mattia has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis  NAM Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJCODES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Epithelium  NOS REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Right breast  N Needle REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Right breast  N Mucin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adipose tissue BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREANBX Separation  NOS Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    1217 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1220 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1223 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJCOPIES TO  CAHILL TERESA M D  NWH RADIOLOGY DEPT  NEWTON  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  617 243 6600 NEWTON CHEH EMILY M D  2000 WASHINGTON ST  NEWTON  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  617 965 7800MARKERS  Breast Disease Related Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORDPROCEDURES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  10 28 08 1218 PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    1218 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   right Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORDFinal  ABBOTT TODD MD   REMOVED_DATE   10 28 08 1425  by MD ABBT MIHOK NICOLE MD        REMOVED_DATE   10 28 08 1430  by MD MIHN                                                                                             , 0.
